; dazzle — the DSSSL transform CLI (the `jade -t sgml|xml -d spec.dsl doc`
; drop-in). Wires the full Stage-6a pipeline end to end: SGML/XML document ->
; opensp parse -> Grove; DSSSL stylesheet -> Interpreter; ProcessContext drives
; the grove through the construction rules into the transform FOTBuilder; the
; top-level output stream goes to stdout (-o is IGNORED for sgml/xml, exactly
; like the reference), while entity/directory flow objects write their own
; files (the codegen use case). fot/rtf/tex write <docbase>.<type> next to the
; document (-o overrides; the file is created BEFORE the document parse, and
; a failed create reports cannotOpenOutputError and skips style processing —
; the reference makeFOTBuilder order).
;
; This is a program, not part of the `define dazzle` package module — it is
; compiled standalone and linked against libdazzle.a + libopensp.a (see
; tests/dazzle/build-cli.sh), exactly as onsgmls.scaly is for opensp.
;
; The CLI is the reference option surface (JadeApp -> DssslApp -> GroveApp ->
; ParserApp -> EntityApp -> CmdLineApp), scanned by the ported getopt clone
; (opensp Options.scaly: clustered shorts, unique-prefix --long names, `--`
; terminator, the ?/-/= signal chars rendered as invalid/ambiguous/erroneous-
; argument errors + the "--help" info line, exit 1). The -b long name is
; always --encoding (GroveApp fixes the internal charset to unicode, so
; internalCharsetIsDocCharset_ is false regardless of SP_CHARSET_FIXED).
;
;   -t TYPE               output type, PREFIX-matched against the reference
;                         table {fot rtf html tex mif sgml xml} (default fot;
;                         empty prefix matches fot; unknown -> unknownType E,
;                         type unchanged). `-t sgml-raw`-style suffixes split
;                         at '-' into backend output options ("raw" wires the
;                         transform RE_/SP_ swap; rtf "95" is unported and
;                         traps LOUDLY, exit 17).
;   -d SYSID[#ID]         the DSSSL spec; #ID selects the style-specification
;                         with that ID (reference splitOffId)
;   -o FILE               output file for fot/rtf/tex/mif (sgml/xml ignore it and
;                         write stdout, like the reference); empty ->
;                         emptyOutputFilename E and the default name applies
;   -V name[=value]       runtime variable define, earliest part wins
;   -G                    debug mode (stack traces, no tail-call replacement)
;   -2                    dsssl2 extensions   -s  strict (RCS) mode
;   -E/--max-errors N     document error limit (0 = unlimited, default 200)
;   -c/--catalog SYSID    must-exist catalog (repeatable; also consulted by
;                         the stylesheet parse, before the bundled DSSSL
;                         catalog); SGML_CATALOG_FILES appends more
;   -C/--catalogs         file arguments are catalogs (DOCUMENT entry)
;   -D/--directory DIR    search DIR for relative sysids; SGML_SEARCH_PATH
;                         appends more
;   -R/--restricted       restricted file reading
;   -w/--warning TYPE     enable warning/validation TYPE (unknownWarning E)
;   -i/--include NAME     define parameter entity NAME as "INCLUDE"
;   -e/-g/-n/-x           reporter options for DOCUMENT diagnostics (open
;                         entities/elements, message numbers, clauses); the
;                         interpreter's own diagnostics don't consult them
;                         (deviation, unused in practice)
;   -a/--activate NAME    activate link type NAME (document parse)
;   -A/--architecture N   parse the document with respect to architecture N
;                         (the ArcEngine transform replaces the event stream
;                         the grove builds from)
;   -b/--encoding NAME    validated (unknownEncoding E); a VALID non-default
;                         encoding does not switch the output encoder yet
;                         (port emits UTF-8, the usual default)
;   -f/--error-file FILE  write diagnostics to FILE (created/truncated)
;   -v/--version          "openjade"/"OpenSP" version banners (run continues)
;   -h/--help             usage text, exit 0 (after a failing -f aborts)
;   SYSID...              document files, merged into ONE document entity
;                         ("-" = stdin <OSFD>0; none = stdin). The default
;                         fot/rtf output name derives from the LAST file
;                         argument (extension replaced when it is at most 4
;                         chars, reference 5-char rule), "jade-out" for pure
;                         stdin.
;
; Without -d the document still parses (exit code = its errors), then
; noSpec ("no DSSSL specification: use -d to specify") reports and style
; processing is skipped. (The reference additionally derives <docbase>.dsl
; for FILE documents, but that path SIGSEGVs in the reference binary —
; probed 2026-07-30 — so the port keeps the sane no-spec behavior there;
; deviation documented.)
;
; Known deviations from the reference binary, all outside ordinary use:
; --long=value with a NON-exact prefix ("--max-err=5") crashes the reference
; (Options::searchLong clobbers sp_ scanning later table entries — att_getopt
; heritage bug); the port parses it correctly. -n message numbers render the
; module as the port's stand-in 0 where the reference prints a raw pointer
; value. -c catalog-open failure counts/ordering may differ (error path).

package scaly 0.1.0
package opensp 0.1.0
package dazzle 0.1.0

use opensp.Parser.Parser
use opensp.ParserState.ParserState
use opensp.ParserOptions.ParserOptions
; ★load-bearing beyond visibility: without the concept in THIS root, a method
; call on a pointer[Syntax] silently answers garbage (the S86 footgun) — that
; cost a debugging round on `general_subst`.
use opensp.Syntax.Syntax
use opensp.Location.InputSource
use opensp.StringC.StringC
use opensp.Options.Options
use opensp.Options.LongOpt
use opensp.EntityManager.EmConfig
use opensp.Message.MessageType
